kimcli

kimcli is a rebranded build of OpenAI Codex CLI 0.144.3
(https://github.com/openai/codex), distributed under the terms of the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). This fork is maintained by Kim
and is not affiliated with or endorsed by OpenAI.

Modifications made in this fork, relative to upstream Codex CLI 0.144.3:

  * Binary identity: the CLI binary is renamed from `codex` to `kimcli`
    (the underlying Cargo package/crate names are unchanged). Running
    `kimcli --version` reports "kimcli 0.144.3 (rebranded codex-cli 0.144.3)".

  * User-visible branding: terminal output, help text, onboarding copy, and
    command examples that referred to "Codex" as a product, or invoked the
    `codex` binary by name, were updated to refer to "Kim" / `kimcli`.
    Functional identifiers are unchanged, including but not limited to:
    environment variable names (e.g. CODEX_HOME, CODEX_API_KEY,
    OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENAI_BASE_URL), the `~/.codex` home directory and its
    layout, config.toml keys and schema, the app-server JSON-RPC wire
    protocol, login/auth flows and "Sign in with ChatGPT" messaging,
    telemetry/OTel tag values, and references to OpenAI's separate Codex
    Desktop application.

  * Self-update permanently disabled: kimcli never checks for or downloads
    an upstream Codex release. The TUI upgrade-check and upgrade-banner
    code paths are stubbed to no-ops, and the `kimcli update` subcommand
    always refuses with a message pointing to
    scripts/install_kimcli.sh in the kim repo, exiting non-zero.

  * Desktop-app install/launch permanently disabled: kimcli never downloads
    or installs OpenAI's Codex Desktop application. The `kimcli app`
    subcommand (which upstream downloads and installs Codex Desktop from
    OpenAI's CDN on macOS, or from the Microsoft Store on Windows) always
    refuses, exiting non-zero, on every platform; the underlying
    installer/launcher code has been removed. Kim's own, separate desktop
    app is not installed or launched by kimcli.

No other functional changes are made by this rebrand.
